diff --git a/docs/development/DEV-TEST-PROD.md b/docs/development/DEV-TEST-PROD.md
index 2caaef93e493bd6b13152d55314b2718ee243262..380d92338adab886788a6cbf24556cff36cd4d4c 100644
--- a/docs/development/DEV-TEST-PROD.md
+++ b/docs/development/DEV-TEST-PROD.md
@@ -57,6 +57,16 @@ Use zero minimum instances, a bounded maximum per service, an approved maximum n
 
 Evaluate preview applicability against the complete PR diff, and TEST against its last successful owned deployment. A documentation commit arriving during an application build must not cancel that build and strand the application change without a current eligible bundle. Documentation-only PRs skip packaging; documentation-only main advances skip it only when the prior deployed TEST application already covers the unchanged inputs. Missing deployment evidence fails safely toward producing a bundle, never toward assuming the application shipped. For an existing DEV preview, reverting all application changes also compares the deployed source so the reverted application replaces the old preview.
 
+### CI receipt compatibility with parallel Arcade validation
+
+The preview controller accepts full Arcade fixture evidence through `scripts/environments/ci_evidence.py`. It does not require duplicate branch-push regressions. For DEV, the latest first-attempt successful PR run must publish `arcade-validation-<tested-merge-SHA>-1`; the receipt's actual checkout source is independently checked against GitHub's current prospective merge, exact base/head parents and Git tree. The merge tree must equal the preview candidate head tree. Otherwise rebase onto current main and rerun; an API run's `head_sha` is not proof that its job checked out that SHA.
+
+The controller reads only fixed-repository GitHub metadata and a bounded JSON receipt ZIP, verifies its SHA-256, and requires every trusted manifest shard, command and stable aggregate to succeed on the expected GitHub-hosted runner. It compares the candidate's workflow, complete `scripts/ci/` subtree and package/lock files with protected main before trusting the receipt writer. Changes to that policy must be reviewed and integrated before a preview can rely on it. Missing installed policy, missing/expired/partial/cancelled evidence, an unrecognized event or source drift fails closed. The controller never executes the candidate's scripts or downloaded receipt. Existing current-head, archive, role-free-server, IAP and cloud identity checks remain independent.
+
+For integrated TEST, only a complete receipt from the exact current-main source's first-attempt push or explicit manual full run is eligible. A successful narrowed main run that reused earlier application evidence cannot stand in for this fresh complete TEST qualification. The manual full path preserves a safe refresh when routine operational/documentation pushes omit gameplay. Reused CI evidence remains useful for release transitions under its separate policy; it does not establish a new deployed TEST observation.
+
+This proof validates source-level fixture coverage, not byte equality with the disconnected preview. `jems-site-bundle` / `bundle.tgz` changes the banner, configuration and service worker and retains its own archive/content identity, provenance checks and deployed smoke. The existing sealed release manifest's eight production regression groups remain unchanged; never relabel the thirteen Arcade shard receipts into those eight groups. The parent-reporting browser gate remains separate. A later authenticated coverage adapter and complete TEST, provider and owner evidence are required before claiming production approval.
+
 ## Permanent TEST and complete experience
 
 TEST must ultimately support Home/navigation, Ready to Play, My Creations, coaching, generation/modification, artwork, coding, Math/Language, parent/profile controls, rewards/progression, the adult workspace and safe saving/recovery. The initial static packaging and browser smoke cover only a subset and must retain that limitation in status.
